{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-12 18:12 PST: OPEN, not claimed. The plan review (Bedrock, 17:58-18:06 PST) returned BLOCK with 3 blocking findings, all the same defect, which I verified in the code:\n- A ticket-free `# mechanism-ok:` reason is rejected by design. `src/rebar/_commands/sunset_markers.py` (_SUNSET_RE) requires every marker reason to open with a ticket id: four-quad, two-quad or 3-word alias. `scripts/_mechanism_delta/compare.py::_marker_errors` fails `--check` with \"names no sunset ticket\" otherwise, and `_partition` admits nothing.\n- The module docstring states this is the point: \"An admission now has to name a SUNSET TICKET, and that ticket cannot close while its marker is still in the tree.\"\n- `config_key::verify.plan_review_engine` has no entry in `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`. The baseline has no write path for new keys (drain_stale only keeps existing ones; no --lock), and AGENTS.md forbids hand-editing it.\n- So the plan's step 1 makes `check_mechanism_delta.py --check` and `make verify` fail. \"Permanent, names no ticket\" conflicts with the ratchet policy, and no wording-only change can satisfy both. The same applies to closing bossy-impish-hoiho, which the close precheck refuses while the marker names it.\nThis is an operator decision, so the plan is unchanged and the ticket unclaimed."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794535656331386386,"uuid":"bea5baa4-d04c-4df1-90f3-4043338ee673"}